    "text": "An interesting observation by Tim Hains is this panicked market is a planned approach by President Trump.\nThis induced panic can push cash into Treasuries, which forces the Fed to slash interest rates in May, and those lower rates give the Fed the ability to refinance TRILLIONS of debt very inexpensively. It also weakens the dollar and drops mortgage rates.\nIt's a genius play. It actually forces companies to build here to dodge tariffs. It also forces farmers to sell more of their products here in the U.S. to bring grocery prices way down - and an interesting housing market if the mortgage rates drop.\n\"Trump Shares Video Saying He's Crashing Market \"On Purpose\"",
